nd linda who  also helped him write the world of ice  and fire and my fever river art director  rhea golden and another book after that  a who's who in westeros and that's just  the books there are also the successor  shows those have taken a ton of my time  and attention this year now i have seen  some comments out there wondering how  much i am involved in these new series  the answer is a lot deeply heavily  involved in every one of the new shows  and while i have been working closely  with some of the fantastic writers and  showrunners ultimately it is up to me to  try to keep the canon and to do all that  i can to help make the new shows great  and i love these stories alright now for  me this was some of the most exciting  news he shared in this massive update we  now have even further confirmation that  george rr martin is heavily involved  with the new shows as you all know this  is something a lot of us have been  worried about i know i've expressed this  myself i was wondering if he was  actually a co-creator on house of the  dragon or if they were only using his  name to help sell the show well it  doesn't really look like i have to worry  about that anymore he's letting us know  that he is helping them as much as he  can now what i like most about what he  said is he's making sure the writers and  showrunners follow his canon hopefully  that means they will adapt every word  that is written instead of making things  up on their own like we saw on game of  thrones with david and dan now they will  have to invent some things on house of  the dragon because it's not a fully  fleshed out story like a game of thrones  was in a song of ice and fire  unfortunately george hasn't written  anywhere near as much about the dance of  dragons but hopefully they will be  adapting every single thing he has  written about that era in westerosi  history alright so let's get back to  what he said in the update  he also says so far i am very excited  house of the dragon has wrapped in  london and is now in post-production  what i have seen i have loved i am eager  to see more i am excited about the other  successor shows as well however i am  dying to tell you about them but i'm not  supposed to  well maybe there are a few things i can  say  things that hbo announced before or at  least hinted at we are developing live  action shows for hbo  and animated shows for hbo max no i  can't tell you how many but it is my  hope that a number of these shows will  get on the air  not all no it's never all but more than  one now some of the ideas we are working  on are quite different in tone in  approach than what has gone before and  that thrills me the world of westeros  and essos is massive and there is room  in it for many different stories about a  wide range of characters now what can i  tell you well let's see bruno heller the  creator and showrunner of rome is  writing his script for the coreless  velaryon series that one started out as  nine voyages but we're now naming it the  sea snake since we wanted to avoid  having several shows with numbers in the  title the other one being ten thousand  ships the series about nymeria amanda  siegel our showrunner has developed a  couple drafts of that one and we are  forging ahead the third of the  live-action shows is dunkin egg helmed  by steve conrad my team and i have had  some great sessions with steve and his  team and we really hit it off he's  determined to do a faithful adaptation  of the stories which is exactly what i  want  these characters and stories are very  special to me the first season will be  an adaptation of the first novella the  hedge knight contrary to what you may  have read online the shows will not be  called dunkin egg which could be  mistaken for a sitcom by viewers  unfamiliar with these stories we're  leaning to naming it a night of the  seven kingdoms for the series title  though the hedge knight has its  partisans as well now over on the  animated side well i'm 